      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1310607699">
          <groundspeak:date>2025-07-14T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP264 Jumpingpound Creek [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I was planning to do a lot more of something today but the widespread rain is not really floating my boat. (Maybe if I owned a boat.) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oh well, I found this cap and a nearby cache this morning before things really got wet. An easy find once you go to the right marker post! &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="685473763">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-11T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP264 Jumpingpound Creek

Out with Brendan714 on a cap adventure... plan A became rain stopped play so we resorted to plan B collecting a few caps on the way back to YYC. After the &quot;newer&quot; 3 sisters cap, a detour for Jumping Pound.... We almost &quot;found&quot; the triangulation corner post my accident..... TFTC. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683863515">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7573673">geoCurious2</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP264 - Jumpingpound Creek&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having discovered that we actually had a few more days to record Brass Caps, we went out today to get some more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I've not cached out in this area before - wide open country, and a warm chinook wind blowing!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684223611">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP264 - Jumpingpound Creek&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, picking up ones we didn't get to earlier! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A busy day today and lots of walking, but a lot of fun!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; I always love driving around in this area! It's so pretty!!  It took us a bit to find the cap since there are quite a few posts to look at! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_shock.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Gotta look at the GPSr first, THEN the post! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683872346">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP264 - Jumpingpound Creek - we thought we had it as we got out of the car, seems there are options here! Once we found the right one, the cap was easy. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
